<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 16 April, from 1457 BCE to 2007.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1457 BCE <span class="tih-ago">569 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thutmose III defeats a Canaanite coalition at Megiddo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pharaoh Thutmose III routed a coalition led by the king of Kadesh at Megiddo, on a date traditionally reckoned to 16 April. His annals give the first detailed account of a battle in recorded history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1746 CE <span class="tih-ago">280 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jacobite army is crushed at Culloden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Government troops under the Duke of Cumberland routed Charles Edward Stuart's army near Inverness in under an hour. It was the last pitched battle on British soil and was followed by harsh repression in the Highlands.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1856 CE <span class="tih-ago">170 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Powers sign the Paris Declaration on maritime law</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting at the Congress of Paris, the great powers agreed to abolish privateering and protect neutral goods at sea. It was the first multilateral treaty codifying the laws of naval warfare.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1917 CE <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lenin arrives at Petrograd's Finland Station</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning from Swiss exile with German help, Vladimir Lenin was greeted by crowds in Petrograd. His call to oppose the Provisional Government set the Bolsheviks on the road to the October Revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1943 CE <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albert Hofmann experiences the effects of LSD by accident</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Working at Sandoz in Basel, chemist Albert Hofmann absorbed a trace of LSD and felt its effects. Three days later, on 19 April, he took a deliberate dose to test it.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2007 CE <span class="tih-ago">19 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gunman kills 32 people at Virginia Tech</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A student shot dead 32 people on the campus in Blacksburg, Virginia, before killing himself. It was then the deadliest shooting by a lone gunman in US history and led to reforms of background checks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li></ol>
